From 251677ec600bfb661e4cfae6e3a31c55a2527ef7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tstoltz <tristan.stoltz@evolvingresonantcocreationism.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 01:30:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Wire conjunctive-mode composition into pathInfoIsUntrusted,
 add the hardened hook caller

Closes the two remaining pieces from the prior checkpoint's amend list:

- LocalStore::pathInfoIsUntrusted composes B (native trust), I (via
  isContentAddressed), and P (the external hook's verdict) per
  signature-authorization-mode:
  - legacy: unchanged behavior exactly, hook never launched even if a
    path is configured (regression-tested by a later functional-test
    scenario, not yet added).
  - conjunctive: content-addressed paths are explicitly refused (not
    silently equivalent to legacy, per the CA-bypass finding from the
    earlier archaeology pass); native refusal short-circuits without
    consulting the hook (conjunctive can only add a requirement); a
    hook Accept verdict is required in addition to native trust.
  Both the pre-download filter (substitution-goal.cc) and post-download
  gate (addToStore) go through this one function via virtual dispatch,
  confirmed by reading the call sites -- no separate substitution-goal.cc
  change needed.
- New src/libutil/authorization-caller.{hh,cc}: AuthorizationHookConfig::validate
  enforces absolute-path and timeout-bound preconditions once, before any
  invocation. invokeSignatureAuthorizationHook spawns the configured hook
  via startProcess + direct execve (no shell, no PATH lookup, cleared
  environment), drains stdout/stderr on reader threads armed before the
  stdin write (closes a deadlock class a naive implementation would hit),
  and enforces a timeout via a separate waiter thread plus a dual
  process-group-and-direct-pid SIGKILL on expiry (the latter closes a
  narrow race where the child hasn't reached its own setpgid(0,0) yet
  when the timeout fires). Output from a failed invocation is never
  inspected -- the timeout branch returns before stdoutResult/stderrResult
  are touched at all. Exit code is checked against the documented {0,10}
  before the response body is parsed at all; anything else is Failure
  regardless of stdout content.

Builds the JSON request via the dynamic-request shape added to
nix-signature-policy in the prior commit (candidates/built_in_decision/
evaluation_context/enforcement_mode only -- no policy or trust_registry
inline).

Registered in src/libutil/meson.build (source) and
src/libutil/include/nix/util/meson.build (installed header).

Verified: `ninja -C build-check` succeeds cleanly across the entire
workspace (301/301), including nix-util-tests and nix-store-tests
linking successfully -- nothing else in the tree broke. First compile
attempt caught two real bugs, not hypothetical ones: this codebase
shadows POSIX read/write with span-based nix::read/nix::write that
throw SystemError on failure, requiring explicit exception handling
around every call site (an uncaught exception escaping a std::thread
body would std::terminate the whole process).
